>>
Rule 1 (input must be a Tensor; suppresses TypeError for non-tensor inputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (float16 (Half) input is not supported; suppresses RuntimeError for 'Half')
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 6
>>
Rule 3 (input must be floating-point: float32 or float64)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 4 (input probabilities must lie in [0, 1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 5 (out tensor, if provided, must match input shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 6 (out tensor, if provided, must have same dtype as input and not be float16)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 6
